NAME='Saturn'
COVER_SUB='Where you build, fear and mature in each sign.'
T=[
('Fall · 2025–28 · 2055–58','Saturn in impetuous Aries, in Mars’s house, is in fall, and Jyotish marks its debilitation here at 20°. Yet the personality imposes itself: with harmony, a certain restraint keeps the Aries impulse under control, with reserve, perseverance, self-control and the strategic gift of a leader, more feared than loved. Karmic astrology reads Saturn as the soul’s debt, and here it is about learning to act with responsibility. The shadow is fear of starting and harshness with yourself. The lesson: courage is a skill you can practise.'),
('Steady · 1998–2001 · 2028–30','Saturn in constant, methodical Taurus gives a realist spirit, slow in decisions. A sense of the right moment may be missing, which can hold back personal and above all economic realisation: you accumulate wealth by a sure, if modestly profitable, means. Jyotish counts Venus as a friend of Saturn. Volguine’s heavy, cooling charcoal, hard to light but long-burning, fits well. Karmic reading: a debt about security and self-worth. The shadow is rigidity and clinging. The lesson: real security cannot be stored.'),
('Disciplined mind · 2000–03 · 2030–32','Saturn in Gemini, when harmonious, gives balance, prudence and circumspection: an independent, individualist nature with will and moral resistance to the trials of life. Intellectual ability, a taste for scientific and literary study, an aptitude for teaching and concentration. Jyotish counts Mercury as a friend of Saturn, so thought is serious and exact. Karmic reading: a debt about words and learning. You may have doubted your intelligence when young. The shadow is anxiety. The lesson: your voice is worth using.'),
('Detriment · 2003–05 · 2032–35','Saturn in the Moon’s house is in detriment, and Jyotish counts the Moon as an enemy of Saturn. It gives patience, reflection, imagination and memory, with a cult of family and high regard for traditional values. Will, obstinacy, intelligence and considerable passive resistance, though the spirit stays restless, with a pull toward history, archaeology and philosophy. Karmic reading: a debt about protection and emotional warmth. The shadow is coldness and fear of dependence. The lesson: allow yourself to receive care.'),
('Detriment · 2005–07 · 2034–37','Saturn in Leo, in the Sun’s house, is in detriment, and Jyotish counts the Sun as an enemy of Saturn. With harmony it gives good psychophysical resistance, determination, strength of spirit and ambition that help overcome life’s trials, with a high sense of responsibility and respectability, reaching prestigious posts. Love and marriage are not favoured. Karmic reading: a debt about being seen and recognised. The shadow is self-doubt and pride. The lesson: you can be seen without being perfect.'),
('Methodical · 2007–10 · 2036–39','Saturn in Virgo, when harmonious, gives excellent organisational ability, practical intelligence and perseverance, with scientific aptitude and a pull toward wide-ranging activity such as teaching and scientific research. You tend to work as a subordinate, with responsibility and precision, respectful of tradition and firm in your convictions. Jyotish counts Mercury as a friend of Saturn. Karmic reading: a debt about service and health. The shadow is perfectionism and overwork. The lesson: rest is part of the process.'),
('Exalted · 2009–12 · 2039–42','Saturn is exalted in Libra, and Jyotish agrees, placing its peak at 20°. It gives excellent physical resistance, psychophysical balance and a reserved, balanced nature, with practical intelligence, a nose for business and an aptitude for legal, economic, commercial and political studies. Good taste and an artistic sense. With age, a spiritual evolution makes you more available and charitable. Karmic reading: a debt of fairness being repaid. The shadow is fear of conflict. The lesson: loyalty is built through honest conversations.'),
('Intense · 2012–15 · 2041–44','Saturn in dark Scorpio, when harmonious, gives a taciturn, cold, slightly misanthropic character. You are more suited to defence than attack, you do not forgive offences, and your physical and moral resistance is tenacious. Sensual but more rational than sentimental, an individualist with medical aptitude and inventiveness. Jyotish counts Mars as an enemy of Saturn. Karmic reading: a debt about power and trust. The shadow is control and emotional armour. The lesson: trust is a risk worth taking.'),
('Serious · 2014–17 · 2044–47','Saturn in Sagittarius, the sign of expansion and of great distances, gives good physical and moral balance, magnanimity, a developed spiritual sense and a religious vocation, especially with the Sun and Jupiter. A conservative by excellence, wary of novelty, you do not admit skipping steps. Jyotish rates Jupiter neutral to Saturn. Karmic reading: a debt about belief and meaning. The shadow is dogma and fear of the unknown. The lesson: faith can include doubt.'),
('Own sign · 2017–20 · 2047–50','Saturn is at home in Capricorn, and Jyotish gives it own-sign strength. It gives a serious, melancholy, grave, hardworking, perseverant and reserved character, aiming at concrete results. Sensitivity is accentuated but feelings are not shown. Ambition is powerful, more rational than sentimental, oriented to moral and intellectual satisfactions. Volguine’s heavy, cooling charcoal is here at its fullest. Karmic reading: a soul that carries responsibility early. The shadow is coldness and overwork. The lesson: authority is strongest when it is humane.'),
('Own sign · 2020–23 · 2050–53','Saturn is also at home in Aquarius, and Jyotish gives it own-sign strength there. When harmonious it gives a determined and energetic character, a sad nature that does not give way and reacts with force to obstacles and adversity, with great imagination, perseverance, courage and a biting wit. Inventiveness suits the intellect. Karmic reading: a soul that serves collective ideals through discipline. The shadow is detachment and rigid thinking. The lesson: tradition and innovation can work together.'),
('Compassionate · 2023–26 · 2052–55','Saturn in Pisces, when positive, gives intuition and a fervent imagination, an inclination to secrecy and to research, and a bent for philosophical and literary study. You love tranquillity and solitude, where you can focus thoughts and solve the most complex situations. Saturn’s strict rationality fuses with sensitivity. Jyotish rates Jupiter neutral to Saturn. Karmic reading: a debt about compassion and release. The shadow is fear and isolation. The lesson: boundaries make compassion sustainable.'),
]
